hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16058","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said, Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Habib ibn Hind ibn Asma al-Aslami, from Hind ibn Asma, he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to my people of Aslam, and said: Order your people to fast this day, the day of Ashura, so whomever you find of them who ate in the first of his day, let him fast the last of it."
"16059","He said, Affan narrated to us, he said, Wuhayb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Hind ibn Harithah, and Hind was of the companions of al-Hudaybiyah, and his brother whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent ordering his people to fast Ashura, and he is Asma ibn Harithah, so Yahya ibn Hind narrated to me, from Asma ibn Harithah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and said: Order your people to fast this day. He said, what if I find them having eaten, he said: Let them complete the last of their day."
